  "response": "Ran `crimes context src/billing.ts --format json` (against the fixture repo). Here's the briefing before touching the file.\n\n## What `src/billing.ts` does\n\nIt's the billing domain module — ~310 lines, five exports, and three locally-declared interfaces (`User`, `InvoiceLine`, `Invoice`):\n\n- **`generateInvoice(user, items, paymentMethod?)`** — lines 50–253, the whole file's centre of gravity. One body that does: id/metadata generation, per-plan line pricing (`pro` 5% / `team` 10% / `enterprise` 20%, with `addon_` SKUs silently exempt), loyalty discount by account age, inline promo-code resolution (`WELCOME10/20`, `BLACKFRIDAY`, `REF_*`), fraud risk scoring → `allow`/`review`/`block`, country tax table, currency selection, invoice assembly, a PII-leaking `console.log` audit line, metrics emission, plaintext email-body composition, and a fake 3-attempt send-retry loop.\n- **`calculateRefundPreview(user, invoice)`** — despite the name, it awaits `saveRefundAudit` and `sendRefundEmail`, then returns `invoice.totalCents`.\n- **`tax(country, subtotalCents)`** — the same country→rate table that's inlined inside `generateInvoice`.\n- **`recommendUpgrade(user)`** — 4-deep nested plan/tenure/country branches returning an upgrade tier string.\n- **`listRecentInvoices()`** — a `TODO` stub returning `[]`.\n\n## Files to read alongside it\n\n| File | Why |\n|---|---|\n| `src/billing.test.ts` | The only likely test. Both of its tests are flagged: `\"renders the enterprise plan\"` has **zero assertions**, `\"creates an invoice\"` uses only a weak matcher. Treat this file as *unprotected*. |\n| `src/api/state.ts` | **Highest-value read.** It re-declares `User` and `Invoice` with the same names but different shapes — `Invoice` disagrees on 6 fields (`userId`, `currency`, `subtotalCents`, `taxCents`, `discountCents`, `createdAt`), `User` on `createdAt`. Nothing in the build checks the two against each other. |\n| `src/routes/settings/billing.tsx`, `docs/billing.md`